---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { ORIGIN, IMAGE_GZ_URL } from "../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="LWOS online demo"
  windowTitle="LWOS Online Demo - Microsoft Internet Explorer"
  path={`${ORIGIN}/demo/`}
  sections={[]}
>

<h2><img src="/assets/gif/spin.gif" alt="">Run LWOS in your browser</h2>
<p>This is the real system, not a screencast: the machine below is
<a href="https://copy.sh/v86/">v86</a>, a whole IBM-PC-compatible computer
emulated in WebAssembly. It downloads the boot image that CI attaches to a
<a href={IMAGE_GZ_URL}>rolling GitHub release</a> (rebuilt on every push to
<code>main</code>), unpacks it in your browser and boots it.</p>

<figure class="crt">
  <div class="demo-shell">
    <div class="demo-bezel">
      <div id="screen" class="demo-screen" tabindex="0" aria-label="Emulated VGA screen; click here, then type">
        <div id="screen-text"></div>
        <canvas id="screen-canvas" style="display:none"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="demo-btns">
      <button class="btn95" id="demo-restart" disabled>Reset</button>
      <button class="btn95" id="demo-fullscreen" disabled>Fullscreen</button>
      <button class="btn95" id="demo-cad" disabled>Ctrl+Alt+Del</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="demo-build">image: latest CI build from GitHub Releases</figcaption>
</figure>

<p><b>Keyboard:</b> click the black screen once, then type &mdash; the emulator
keeps the keys from then on. Click outside or press <kbd>Esc</kbd> to give them
back to the page.</p>

<hr>

<h2>How it works</h2>
<p>Every push to <code>main</code> makes CI rebuild the image and overwrite
the same release asset, so the machine always boots the latest build.</p>

<hr>

<h2>Credits</h2>
<ul class="links plain">
  <li><a href="https://github.com/copy/v86">v86</a> &mdash; x86 emulator in WebAssembly, BSD-2-Clause (<a href="/vendor/v86/LICENSE-v86">license</a>)</li>
  <li><a href="https://github.com/qemu/seabios">SeaBIOS</a> and <a href="https://www.nongnu.org/vgabios/">VGABIOS</a> &mdash; the BIOS images v86 boots with, LGPL</li>
</ul>

</SiteLayout>

<script>
  import "../scripts/demo.js";
</script>
